// below however long the run takes and whenever it starts. The offset is elapsed
// time, which keeps timestamp order equal to write order -- a synthetic window
// would put "newest" at the window's end rather than at the row just written,
// and the read-after-write probe reads the newest rows.
//
// GENERATED_AT has to be baked in rather than read here: k6 runs this init
